"""Lesson 15 student pages, checked source excerpts and UML sequence."""
STYLE+='''select{font:700 21px/1.5 "Segoe UI";padding:16px;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;width:100%}#custom{width:24px;height:24px}#fixture-content{white-space:pre-wrap;font:20px/1.6 Consolas,monospace;color:var(--ink);background:var(--soft);padding:24px;border-radius:16px;max-height:420px;overflow:auto}#notice:empty{display:none}.markdown-body{white-space:normal!important}.markdown-body li{margin:12px 0}#events li{font-size:19px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.json-view{max-height:460px}.workflow-step{scroll-margin-top:20px}'''
(PUBLIC/'style.css').write_text(STYLE,encoding='utf-8')
learn=[('Write lasting project knowledge','Use CLAUDE.md for conventions, architecture, build/test commands and compact summary guidance. Keep one-off task instructions in the task prompt.'),('Load the right source','project loads project/parent CLAUDE.md and rules; user loads personal instructions and rules; local loads CLAUDE.local.md. Omission and an explicit empty list are distinct.'),('Combine non-conflicting layers','Loaded instruction layers are additive. This lab uses different marker lines so students can observe compliance without inventing a universal precedence ladder.'),('Discover child instructions on demand','The child experiment reads feature/data.md while the working directory remains the project root. Observe whether the child CLAUDE.md instruction appears after that Read.'),('Observe real compaction','The compaction mode creates one owned persisted session, sends /compact, observes compact_boundary, then resumes the same session and checks the actual answer. Continued compliance is not a wire-level proof of reinjection.'),('Separate instructions from permissions','CLAUDE.md works with custom and preset system prompts as conversation context. A host Read guard independently limits tools to classroom data files. Markers describe model compliance, not a complete instruction audit.')]
body='''<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Write</b><p>Project knowledge and rules</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Load</b><p>Select matching sources</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Verify</b><p>Actual reads and responses</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Which project instructions reach the agent?</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Project-memory experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="project">Project + parent + API rule</option><option value="none">No filesystem sources · []</option><option value="combined">User + project sources</option><option value="defaults">Omit settingSources · all three defaults</option><option value="disabled">Project source + disable all CLAUDE.md</option><option value="child">Read feature/data.md · discover child rule</option><option value="compact">Summary → actual /compact → recall</option></select><label><input id="custom" type="checkbox"> Use a custom system prompt instead of the coding preset</label><p class="note">The fixed task summarizes a read-only catalogue project and follows already-loaded response rules. Expected marker values and fixture contents are never placed in the task prompt. Only data.md or feature/data.md can be read by model tools.</p><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run the project-rules experiment →</button></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>Latest SDK cost estimate: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p class="meta">Safe option projection. Full process environment and expanded internal prompt are not returned. Each experiment uses fresh owned paths; compact alone resumes its own session.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Independent observations</h2><p id="boundary">No compaction boundary observed yet.</p><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Read paths come from PostToolUse. Markers are extracted from actual text, not inserted into it. A missing marker alone does not prove a file was absent. The latest cost estimate may include restored session usage; do not sum resumed totals as new spend.</p></section><section class="step" id="fixtures-panel"><h2>Inspect the trusted instruction files</h2><label for="fixture">File location</label><select id="fixture"></select><div id="fixture-content" role="region" aria-label="Instruction file contents">Run an experiment to inspect its safe fixtures.</div><p>These contents are a host-rendered student view, not task-prompt injection. The model cannot Read these instruction files using tools.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual session initialization</h2><pre><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s runs</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Custom prompt</th><th>Markers returned</th><th>Completed reads</th><th>Compact boundaries</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages</h2><ul id="events"></ul></section>'''
document('/','Persistent <em>project instructions.</em>','Explore CLAUDE.md, rules, source selection, child discovery and actual compaction.',body,'<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Write once, load deliberately, then verify actual application evidence.',cards(learn)+actions(('/run.html','Configure and run →'),('/architecture.html','Explore the UML →')))
env=(APP/'.env.example').read_text(encoding='utf-8').strip()
runsteps=[('Prepare the project','Use Node.js 24+, npm, Git Bash on Windows if required, and an Anthropic account with access to the configured model.','cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson15-project-rules'),('Install and create your .env','Preserve an existing file. Copy the example only when needed, and enter your own API key locally.','npm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) {\n  Copy-Item .env.example .env\n}\nnotepad .env'),('Start and compare project sources','Keep the terminal running. Open port 3115. Run Project first, then No filesystem sources. Inspect markers, data reads and the safe fixture viewer.','npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3115'),('Combine additive locations','Run User + project with a custom prompt. Then run omitted defaults and compare the local marker as well. These non-conflicting fixtures do not prove a universal precedence order.','npm run sample:env -- combined --custom'),('Test disabled and child instructions','Run the disable flag case. Then read feature/data.md in the child experiment and compare the observed child rule marker.','npm run sample:env -- disabled\nnpm run sample:env -- child'),('Observe compaction in the same session','Run Summary → compact → recall. Wait for the entire three-phase experiment. Verify an actual boundary and matching session IDs, then inspect the final returned markers.','npm run sample:env -- compact\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>The npm scripts load the optional .env explicitly. Existing shell variables take precedence. Restart after edits. No Managed Agents agent or environment ID is needed.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>If this app is already listening, startup prints its URL. If another service occupies the port, change PORT or stop that service. On Windows set CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH to the installed bash.exe if necessary. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. Check key/model access if a real query fails; errors are never replaced by a saved answer.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install, set your key, then compare fresh real SDK sessions.',body)
specs=[('Validate the chosen experiment', 'src/agent.ts', 'config=validateConfig(config);', 'Only listed source experiments and a boolean custom-prompt choice are accepted. The browser cannot submit arbitrary paths or instruction text.', 0, 1), ('Resolve owned instruction locations', 'src/agent.ts', 'return { parent: resolve(root, "organization"),', 'Each run gets an owned parent/project tree plus private home and SDK configuration paths. These classroom directories are not an OS sandbox.', 1, 4), ('Write project, parent and personal fixtures', 'src/agent.ts', 'for (const file of files) await writeFile', 'The host writes non-conflicting CLAUDE.md and rule files. Their contents are visible to students but are not copied into the task prompt.', 1, 4), ('Select the intended filesystem sources', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (mode === "defaults") return undefined;', 'Omission preserves runtime defaults. An empty list skips user/project/local sources. Named arrays enable only the selected levels.', 1, 2), ('Disable CLAUDE.md independently', 'src/agent.ts', '...(config.mode === "disabled" ?', 'The disable environment flag is independent of the selected project source. The actual result remains an observation of this pinned runtime.', 1, 2), ('Keep system prompt and project memory separate', 'src/agent.ts', 'systemPrompt: config.custom', 'The custom and preset forms are application roles. CLAUDE.md and rules are separate conversation context loaded through settingSources.', 1, 2), ('Guard model tool reads', 'src/agent.ts', 'return ["data.md", "feature/data.md"].some', 'The host permits only the exact owned data files. Model tools cannot Read instruction files to imitate implicit loading.', 2, 1), ('Choose root data or child data', 'src/agent.ts', ': config.mode === "child" ?', 'The child task reads feature/data.md while cwd remains the project root. That file access can trigger on-demand child instructions.', 1, 2), ('Start or resume the owned query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run = query({prompt,options:', 'Only the session ID observed inside this run can be resumed. The browser cannot attach to an arbitrary remote session.', 1, 2), ('Preserve session identity across phases', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (sessionId && message.session_id !== sessionId)', 'Summary, compaction and recall retain the same observed session identity. A mismatch is an error rather than a hidden fresh query.', 2, 1), ('Observe a real compaction boundary', 'src/agent.ts', 'compactBoundaries++;', 'A system compact_boundary message records actual compaction. Continued instruction compliance is checked in the following real query; this is not a wire-level prompt capture.', 2, 1), ('Keep actual final markers and phase outcomes', 'src/agent.ts', 'phases.push({phase,status,markers:', 'Extract markers from actual SDK text and retain phase outcomes. Missing compliance is never replaced with an expected answer.', 2, 1), ('Format the answer and expose safe fixture contents', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer") renderMarkdown', 'The browser renders sanitized Markdown. Instruction files are shown separately as plain, readable text for students.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK + Claude','Read guard','Private files']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={2:2,4:4,11:2}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
xs=[170,520,870,1220,1570];svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1740" height="1600" viewBox="0 0 1740 1600"><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1740" height="1600" fill="#f4f9ff"/><text x="40" y="52" font-family="Arial" font-size="34" fill="#101a44">Lesson 15 · Write rules → load project context → observe actual SDK evidence</text>']
for x,label,colour in zip(xs,lanes,['#087fff','#8838ff','#00a977','#8838ff','#ee5425']):svg.append(f'<rect x="{x-150}" y="90" width="300" height="80" rx="16" fill="{colour}"/><text x="{x}" y="139" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-size="27" fill="white">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x} 170 V1550" stroke="#aec6df" stroke-dasharray="8 7"/>')
for i,(a,b,label) in enumerate(arrows):
 x1,x2=xs[a],xs[b];y=245+i*98;svg.append(f'<text x="{min(x1,x2)+10}" y="{y-18}" fill="#142d53" font-family="Arial" font-size="24">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x1} {y} H{x2}" stroke="#087fff" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>')
(PUBLIC/'architecture.svg').write_text(''.join(svg)+'</svg>',encoding='utf-8')
walk=''
for s in steps:walk+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{s["number"]:02}"><span class="number">{s["number"]:02}</span><h3>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]} · selected source; surrounding code omitted</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen prompt selection and query workflow steps"></div>'+walk)
reference=[('Seven load locations', 'Project root CLAUDE.md or .claude/CLAUDE.md; project rules and parent rules; parent CLAUDE.md; child CLAUDE.md on demand; local CLAUDE.local.md; private user CLAUDE.md; and user rules. This lab creates all seven categories, not every alternative file spelling.'), ('Additive instructions', 'All selected layers can appear together. Avoid conflicts or state intended precedence explicitly in your own project text. This lab uses independent marker lines rather than conflicting language or package-manager rules.'), ('Compaction and limits', 'Project-root CLAUDE.md is re-read after compaction. Nested instruction files and path-scoped rules must load again on demand. The live exercise observes a real boundary and subsequent compliance, not the full provider request payload. Keep files lean; caching and perfect model compliance are not guaranteed.'), ('What belongs in CLAUDE.md', 'Repository conventions, architecture, build/test commands, lasting constraints and focused summary guidance. Write task-specific requests in user input and application-specific persona instructions in systemPrompt.'), ('Configuration boundaries', 'The app uses private config/home paths, disables auto memory and connector discovery, and configures strict MCP. settingSources is not an OS sandbox and does not remove managed policy. Local personal notes should remain uncommitted.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Follow actual application code and distinguish reference topics from live experiments.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 15 · CLAUDE.md and project rules\n\nBased on Lesson15_CLAUDE_md_and_Project_Rules.pptx. Five linked web pages, large text, formatted answers and 13 source-linked UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson15-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson15-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations, use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson15-project-rules` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3115 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+ and model access are required.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file or copy .env.example. Enter your key locally; do not commit it. Restart after edits. Shell values take precedence over the optional file loaded by npm start.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nOn Windows, set the Git Bash path if needed. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. A second start recognizes this app; change PORT if another service occupies it.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'+''.join(f'{i}. {a}: {b}\n' for i,(a,b,c) in enumerate(runsteps[3:],1))+'\n```powershell\nnpm run sample:env -- project\nnpm run sample:env -- none\nnpm run sample:env -- combined --custom\nnpm run sample:env -- compact\nnpm test\n```\n\n`sample` uses only the launching shell environment; `sample:env` loads the optional file. All queries are real and read-only. Prompt and context are fixed classroom choices, not arbitrary browser-supplied source paths.\n\n## How the app was built\n\n'
for s in steps:readme+=f'### {s["number"]}. {s["title"]}\n\n{s["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{s["source"]}`, lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]}. Selected excerpt.\n\n```typescript\n{s["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\nThe app never exposes the expanded internal prompt or inherited environment. Marker flags describe actual text, not complete instruction audits. Private classroom directories are not an OS sandbox. Media, .env, dependencies and runtime files are excluded from Git.\n\n## References\n\n- [Project memory and compaction](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory)\n- [Official filesystem features guide](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/modifying-project-rules)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 15 pages and 13 checked UML source snippets.')
